From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Yevhen Salitrynskyi <ysalitrynskyi@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 25 Oct 2026 09:39:12 -0400
Subject: feat: History and Downloads as panels in the sidebar (S-98)

History and Downloads open in the sidebar's column, in the tab list's
place, from Cmd+Y / Ctrl+H, Shift+Cmd+J / Opt+Cmd+L / Ctrl+J, the menus,
the command bar's rows and the bottom row's buttons
(docs/features/sidebar-panels.md Pn1-Pn16). A new chrome://stedding-library
page reuses Chromium's History and Downloads handlers and adds open in the
window, Copy File and Move to Trash (Pn7, Pn10, Pn11). The panel's web
view forwards unhandled keys to the window, never navigates away, and is
dropped only after the call that closed it returns (Pn1, Pn5, Pn7). A
panel draws a narrow sidebar 340 DIP wide without writing the user's
width, slides a rail out and holds it (Pn4). The downloads button opens
the Downloads panel and nudges when a download finishes (Pn2, Pn13); a
History button sits beside it and the Archived row wears an archive box
(Pn15, sidebar Y44). Nothing is fetched (Pn8). Setting
stedding.sidebar.library_panels, on by default (Pn14, settings T34).

Why: the operator asked in chat on 2026-10-25 for the next big features
to be built; BACKLOG S-98 asks for History and Downloads in the sidebar's
column instead of as pages.
Removable when: the profile setting turns it off per user; the code goes
only if Chromium's own side panel comes to host both lists in the
sidebar's column.
